translated_text:
Article 8

1. In efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence, the City Government is obliged to:a. guarantee the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations; b. establish and implement policy programs and activities for the protection of the rights of women and children; c. facilitate the formation of community organizations concerned with women and children;
d. cooperate with the community and/or community organizations and the private sector in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. carry out rehabilitation and empowerment of women and children who are victims of acts of violence; f. provide special protection to women and children victims of various acts of violence; andg. take preventive action in order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children. (2) The responsibility in efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.
3. Further provisions regarding the obligations of the City Government as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

