(1) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (2) letter a aim to:
a. assist victims in recognizing their problems and finding effective ways to overcome them independently;
b. empower victims to determine their future; c. provide moral support for victims in facing the legal process they are undergoing; andd. make victims feel accepted in the community environment. (2) Counseling services are conducted by social rehabilitation officers who are gender responsive, consisting of:a. counselors who have obtained certificates;
b. psychologists; andc. psychiatrists.
3. Counseling services are conducted in places that guarantee a sense of security, comfort and confidentiality of information from victims. (4) The stages of counseling services include:a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case discussion; andd. site visits.
